2025-05-01 03:42:50 - Thread-1597 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage
• races."year": season we need to restrict to the 1950‑1959 decade  
• races."round": lets us decide which of a driver’s races in that season was first / last  
• races."race_id": primary key that ties the season / round to results  
• results."race_id": foreign key → join to races   
• results."driver_id": identify the driver  
• results."constructor_id": identify which constructor the driver used in that race  
• drivers."driver_id": join to get the driver’s name  
• drivers."forename", drivers."surname": build readable full‑name output  
• constructors."constructor_id", constructors."name": (optional) readable constructor name  

Main conditions that will be required  
1. races."year" BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959  
2. COUNT(DISTINCT races."round") ≥ 2 for each (driver, year) pair  
3. MIN(races."round") and MAX(races."round") for that pair must both have the same constructor_id  

Below are ten exploratory → increasingly complex queries (all read‑only, using DISTINCT where helpful, each capped with LIMIT 20).  
Run them in order to validate every step and finally obtain the requested list.

```sql
-- 1) Quick look at which seasons are in the 1950s
SELECT DISTINCT r."year"
FROM races AS r
WHERE r."year" BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
ORDER BY r."year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Which drivers appear in results during the 1950s? (just ids for now)
SELECT DISTINCT res."driver_id"
FROM results AS res
JOIN races  AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
WHERE r."year" BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Same as #2 but with driver names
SELECT DISTINCT d."driver_id",
       d."forename" || ' ' || d."surname" AS driver_name
FROM results  AS res
JOIN races    AS r  ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
JOIN drivers  AS d  ON d."driver_id" = res."driver_id"
WHERE r."year" BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
ORDER BY d."driver_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) For each driver‑season, how many different race rounds did they start?
SELECT res."driver_id",
       r."year",
       COUNT(DISTINCT r."round") AS rounds_entered
FROM results AS res
JOIN races   AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
WHERE r."year" BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
GROUP BY res."driver_id", r."year"
HAVING rounds_entered >= 2
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Add constructor used in every race so we can see variability
SELECT res."driver_id",
       r."year",
       r."round",
       res."constructor_id"
FROM results AS res
JOIN races   AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
WHERE r."year" BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
ORDER BY res."driver_id", r."year", r."round"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Find the constructor in the FIRST race of each driver‑season
WITH first_race AS (
  SELECT res."driver_id",
         r."year",
         MIN(r."round") AS first_round
  FROM results AS res
  JOIN races   AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
  WHERE r."year" BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
  GROUP BY res."driver_id", r."year"
)
SELECT fr."driver_id",
       fr."year",
       res."constructor_id" AS first_constructor_id
FROM first_race AS fr
JOIN results    AS res
      ON res."driver_id" = fr."driver_id"
     AND res."race_id"   = (
           SELECT r2."race_id"
           FROM races AS r2
           WHERE r2."year"  = fr."year"
             AND r2."round" = fr."first_round"
           LIMIT 1
         )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Same technique for the LAST race of each driver‑season
WITH last_race AS (
  SELECT res."driver_id",
         r."year",
         MAX(r."round") AS last_round
  FROM results AS res
  JOIN races   AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
  WHERE r."year" BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
  GROUP BY res."driver_id", r."year"
)
SELECT lr."driver_id",
       lr."year",
       res."constructor_id" AS last_constructor_id
FROM last_race AS lr
JOIN results   AS res
      ON res."driver_id" = lr."driver_id"
     AND res."race_id"   = (
           SELECT r2."race_id"
           FROM races AS r2
           WHERE r2."year"  = lr."year"
             AND r2."round" = lr."last_round"
           LIMIT 1
         )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Combine first & last constructor, keep only rows where they match
WITH summary AS (
  SELECT res."driver_id",
         r."year",
         MIN(r."round") AS first_round,
         MAX(r."round") AS last_round,
         COUNT(DISTINCT r."round") AS rounds_entered
  FROM results AS res
  JOIN races   AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
  WHERE r."year" BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
  GROUP BY res."driver_id", r."year"
  HAVING rounds_entered >= 2
),
first_const AS (
  SELECT s."driver_id", s."year", res."constructor_id" AS first_c
  FROM summary AS s
  JOIN races   AS r   ON r."year" = s."year"  AND r."round" = s."first_round"
  JOIN results AS res ON res."race_id" = r."race_id" AND res."driver_id" = s."driver_id"
),
last_const AS (
  SELECT s."driver_id", s."year", res."constructor_id" AS last_c
  FROM summary AS s
  JOIN races   AS r   ON r."year" = s."year"  AND r."round" = s."last_round"
  JOIN results AS res ON res."race_id" = r."race_id" AND res."driver_id" = s."driver_id"
)
SELECT s."driver_id", s."year",
       fc.first_c, lc.last_c, s.rounds_entered
FROM summary     AS s
JOIN first_const AS fc ON fc."driver_id" = s."driver_id" AND fc."year" = s."year"
JOIN last_const  AS lc ON lc."driver_id" = s."driver_id" AND lc."year" = s."year"
WHERE fc.first_c = lc.last_c
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Bring in readable driver & constructor names for the qualifying rows
WITH summary AS (
  SELECT res."driver_id",
         r."year",
         MIN(r."round") AS first_round,
         MAX(r."round") AS last_round,
         COUNT(DISTINCT r."round") AS rounds_entered
  FROM results AS res
  JOIN races   AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
  WHERE r."year" BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
  GROUP BY res."driver_id", r."year"
  HAVING rounds_entered >= 2
),
first_const AS (
  SELECT s."driver_id", s."year", res."constructor_id" AS constructor_id
  FROM summary AS s
  JOIN races   AS r   ON r."year" = s."year"  AND r."round" = s."first_round"
  JOIN results AS res ON res."race_id" = r."race_id" AND res."driver_id" = s."driver_id"
),
last_const AS (
  SELECT s."driver_id", s."year", res."constructor_id" AS constructor_id
  FROM summary AS s
  JOIN races   AS r   ON r."year" = s."year"  AND r."round" = s."last_round"
  JOIN results AS res ON res."race_id" = r."race_id" AND res."driver_id" = s."driver_id"
)
SELECT DISTINCT d."forename" || ' ' || d."surname"  AS driver_name,
       s."year",
       c."name"                                     AS constructor_name,
       s.rounds_entered
FROM summary     AS s
JOIN first_const AS fc ON fc."driver_id" = s."driver_id" AND fc."year" = s."year"
JOIN last_const  AS lc ON lc."driver_id" = s."driver_id" AND lc."year" = s."year"
JOIN drivers     AS d  ON d."driver_id" = s."driver_id"
JOIN constructors AS c ON c."constructor_id" = fc."constructor_id"
WHERE fc."constructor_id" = lc."constructor_id"
ORDER BY s."year", driver_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) FINAL ANSWER: complete list of all driver‑season pairs that meet every criterion
WITH summary AS (
  SELECT res."driver_id",
         r."year",
         MIN(r."round") AS first_round,
         MAX(r."round") AS last_round,
         COUNT(DISTINCT r."round") AS rounds_entered
  FROM results AS res
  JOIN races   AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
  WHERE r."year" BETWEEN 1950 AND 1959
  GROUP BY res."driver_id", r."year"
  HAVING rounds_entered >= 2
),
first_const AS (
  SELECT s."driver_id", s."year", res."constructor_id" AS constructor_id
  FROM summary AS s
  JOIN races   AS r   ON r."year" = s."year"  AND r."round" = s."first_round"
  JOIN results AS res ON res."race_id" = r."race_id" AND res."driver_id" = s."driver_id"
),
last_const AS (
  SELECT s."driver_id", s."year", res."constructor_id" AS constructor_id
  FROM summary AS s
  JOIN races   AS r   ON r."year" = s."year"  AND r."round" = s."last_round"
  JOIN results AS res ON res."race_id" = r."race_id" AND res."driver_id" = s."driver_id"
)
SELECT DISTINCT d."forename" || ' ' || d."surname"  AS driver_name,
       s."year",
       c."name"                                     AS constructor_name,
       s.rounds_entered
FROM summary     AS s
JOIN first_const AS fc ON fc."driver_id" = s."driver_id" AND fc."year" = s."year"
JOIN last_const  AS lc ON lc."driver_id" = s."driver_id" AND lc."year" = s."year"
JOIN drivers     AS d  ON d."driver_id" = s."driver_id"
JOIN constructors AS c ON c."constructor_id" = fc."constructor_id"
WHERE fc."constructor_id" = lc."constructor_id"
ORDER BY s."year", driver_name
LIMIT 20;
```

Each query progressively builds the logic you need—from identifying 1950‑era data, to confirming race counts, to checking constructor consistency, and finally listing the qualifying drivers with readable names.
